Introduction

The NXE Availability team within the Performance and Integration department at ASML is dedicated to ensuring that our NXE scanners meet our customers' needs for high-volume manufacturing. We focus on optimizing all disturbances and inefficiencies that hamper our systems' availability for production. To gain valuable insights, we make use of various large data sets that our systems continuously produce.

Your Assignment

For this internship assignment, you will work with industrial engineers and professionals and you will interact with different teams. As an intern in our team, you will be contributing to our data and analysis infrastructure to get the most out of the available data sources. Your tasks may include:

Learn and understand the work we do;

Propose and develop solutions for documenting and visualizing data, which will be used by project leads in their report-outs (e.g., dashboards in Power BI, Spotfire, or other visualization tools);

Support the project leads in updating data and improving the roadmap planning;

Dashboarding: create insightful overviews of linked data and present these to internal stakeholders;

Organize the knowledge-management for the Availability technical competence.

Through these activities, this internship offers a unique opportunity to learn how NXE systems are used by our customers and contribute to creating more value. As part of the Source Availability team, you will help in steering the organization in the right direction in terms of availability improvements. As an intern, you will gain in-depth knowledge on the topic and contribute to our roadmap and documenting (sometimes through reverse engineering) various topics in our availability roadmap.

